{"route":"/docs/4.6/utilities/overflow/","version":"4.6","renderedVersion":"4.6","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Overflow","level":1},"lead":{"id":"page--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/blob/v4.6.2/site/content/docs/4.6/utilities/overflow.md\">View on GitHub</a>"},"blocks":[{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Use these shorthand utilities for quickly configuring how content overflows an element."},{"id":"content--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Barebones <code>overflow</code> functionality is provided for two values by default, and they are not responsive."},{"id":"content--example-1","type":"demo","key":"3e824044fc3364bfcde7","height":174},{"id":"content--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"overflow-auto\">...</div>\n<div class=\"overflow-hidden\">...</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"content--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Using Sass variables, you may customize the overflow utilities by changing the <code>$overflows</code> variable in <code>_variables.scss</code>."}],"demos":[{"key":"3e824044fc3364bfcde7","html":"\n  <div class=\"overflow-auto p-3 mb-3 mb-md-0 mr-md-3 bg-light\" style=\"max-width: 260px; max-height: 100px;\">\n    This is an example of using <code>.overflow-auto</code> on an element with set width and height dimensions. By design, this content will vertically scroll.\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"overflow-hidden p-3 bg-light\" style=\"max-width: 260px; max-height: 100px;\">\n    This is an example of using <code>.overflow-hidden</code> on an element with set width and height dimensions.\n  </div>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example d-md-flex"},"sprite":""}],"nav":[{"en":"Getting started","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/getting-started/introduction/"},{"en":"Layout","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/layout/overview/"},{"en":"Content","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.6/content/reboot/"},{"en":"Components","href":"https://getbootst